**Design Notes:**  
The Galois LFSR implementation uses a synchronous reset to initialize the register to 32'h1. The feedback mechanism XORs tap bits (32, 22, 2, 1) with the LSB (q[0]) to generate the next state. The register shifts right, with the MSB set to the feedback value. The shift operation uses non-blocking assignments to avoid race conditions, and the feedback calculation is performed before the shift to ensure correct state transitions.

